  "id": "COMPOUND:9755 - PROTEIN:6020",
  "verbalization": "Dalotuzumab is implicated in the regulation of PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through a series of molecular interactions involving UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. This enzyme serves as a common target for multiple compounds, including Acetamide, Sennoside D, and 9-Isovaleroxy Balanophonin, all of which are known to interact with CDC2L1. The evidence suggests that Dalotuzumab may exert its effects by modulating the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, which in turn influences the downstream signaling of CDC2L1. The shared target of these compounds points to a potential mechanism where Dalotuzumab could either directly or indirectly regulate CDC2L1 through the activation or inhibition of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10 as a mediator in the drug's action on CDC2L1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
